# LEXOS Security and Privacy Rules

Never commit secrets.

Never expose the Supabase service-role key client-side.

Never place real legal/client data in tests, fixtures, examples, screenshots, logs, or seed files.

Use fake/demo data only.

Evidence buckets must not be public by default.

Original evidence, extraction artifacts, transcripts, visual descriptions, OCR, markdown, JSON, embeddings, prompts, and generated artifacts inherit privilege/confidentiality sensitivity from their source material unless explicitly reviewed and reclassified.

Derived artifacts inherit source evidence security labels.

Prompt context must label:

- QA-flagged extraction;
- low-confidence extraction;
- raw OCR fallback;
- human-review-required content;
- privilege/confidentiality status.

Logs must not store full privileged content unless explicitly secured and justified.

Avoid storing full prompts containing privileged evidence in insecure logs.

Use scoped excerpts where possible.

Do not create autonomous external legal communication in MVP.

Do not create court filing tools in MVP.

Do not create external email/opposing counsel/client communication tools unless explicitly instructed and governed.

Do not create or enable global retrieval by default.

Do not allow user interfaces to imply that drafts are externally approved.

Stop and report if implementation requires:

- production credentials;
- real legal data;
- broad public storage access;
- external transmission of legal material;
- weakening privilege/confidentiality labels;
- client/matter isolation exceptions.
